{title: 120 - There's a Song in the Air}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #120 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 120}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]There’s a song [D7/A]in the air!
[G]There’s a star in [D/A]the sky!
[D7]There’s [G]a mother’s [D/A]deep prayer
[D/A]And a [Am]baby’s [D]low cry!
[D7]And the [G]star rains its fire
[D7/A]while the beautiful sing,
[D7]For the [Em/G]manger [G]of [Am/C]Bethlehem
[D7]cradles a [G]King!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]There's a tumult [D7]of joy
[G]O'er the wonderful [D/A]birth,
[D7]For the [G]virgin's [D/A]sweet boy
[D/A]Is the [Am]Lord of [D]the earth.
[D7]Aye! the [G]star rains its fire
[D7/A]while the beautiful sing,
[D7]For the [Em/G]manger [G]of [Am/C]Bethlehem
[D7]cradles a [G]King!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]In the light of [D7]that star
[G]Lie the ages [D/A]impearled;
[D7]And that [G]song from [D/A]afar
[D/A]Has swept [Am]over [D]the world.
[D7]Every [G]hearth is aflame
[D7/A]and the beautiful sing
[D7]In the [Em/G]homes [G]of [Am/C]the [C]nations
[D7]that Jesus is [G]King!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]We rejoice in [D7]the light,
[G]And we echo [D/A]the song
[D7]That comes [G]down [D/A]through the night
[D7]From the [G]heavenly throng.
[D7/A]Aye! we shout to the lovely evangel they bring,
[D7]And we [Em/G]greet [G]in [Am/C]His [C]cradle
[D7]our Savior and [G]King!
{end_of_verse}
